# Carries a per-rule allowlist for the upstream felddy maintainer's public
# contact address, which appears all through inherited history (package.json,
# pyproject.toml, Dockerfile, issue templates, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) and is not
# leaked PII. The template has no such entry, so syncing this file strips the
# allowlist and the full-history gitleaks scan in secret-scan.yml starts
# flagging it. Verified against sync PR #59, which proposed exactly that.
.gitleaks.toml
# Private-repo gate ignores for semgrep/container-scan/dependency-review were
# removed 2026-07-05 (repo is public; sync may revert the now-inert gates).
# codeql-analysis.yml stays ignored: this fork's language matrix tracks its own
# sources (actions, javascript-typescript, python) rather than the template's,
# and the felddy diagnostics job has no upstream equivalent.
.github/workflows/codeql-analysis.yml
# Carries this fork's Obsidian-vault bind mount (source→/home/node/DnD); the
# vault is the durable source of truth (see README + docs/PROJECT.md). A bind
# mount can only be declared in devcontainer.json, so this one divergence cannot
# be moved anywhere else — the template cannot carry it either, since a bind to a
# host path that does not exist breaks container start for every other
# derivative. The postStartCommand symlink that used to live here moved into
# scripts/project-setup.sh, so the chain now matches the template's apart from
# the trailing hook call.
#
# TRADE-OFF: this file no longer receives upstream template updates. It is the
# one ignore entry that costs real security coverage, so diff it against the
# template whenever the template's devcontainer changes:
#   diff <(gh api repos/Moon-Knight13/claude_template_repo/contents/.devcontainer/devcontainer.json \
#            --jq .content | base64 -d) .devcontainer/devcontainer.json
# Carries one project-owned egress allowlist entry: api.open5e.com, the 5e rules
# API the content pipeline verifies authored stat blocks against. Sync merges
# with -X theirs, so without this the entry is silently reverted and the next
# refresh fails with a bare connection error long after anyone remembers why.
#
# TRADE-OFF, and it is a bigger one than devcontainer.json above: this is a
# SECURITY CONTROL, so pinning it means upstream hardening of the firewall stops
# arriving. Diff it against the template whenever the template's firewall
# changes, and port improvements by hand:
#   diff <(gh api repos/Moon-Knight13/claude_template_repo/contents/.devcontainer/init-firewall.sh \
#            --jq .content | base64 -d) .devcontainer/init-firewall.sh
# Expect exactly one hunk: the optional-domains block.
#
# The allowlist entry is a CONVENIENCE, not a dependency — the pipeline reads a
# committed cache under content/reference/ and needs no network for a normal
# build or for CI. If this entry is ever lost, only an in-container refresh
# breaks, and it can be run from the host instead.
.devcontainer/init-firewall.sh
# Expect exactly two hunks: the mounts entry, and nothing else.
.devcontainer/devcontainer.json

